  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 345 AM CDT Fri Jul 24 2026\n\nThe extended is fairly straightforward, hot, and dry, with \ntemperatures most locations climbing into the triple digits each \nafternoon, and lows remaining unseasonably warm each night due to \nthe LLJ.  The upper ridge will park itself more or less just east of \nthe Four Corners, with minor temperature fluctuations dependent on \nwhere it shifts each day.  At this time, Monday looks to be the \nwarmest day this forecast, similar to yesterday's highs.  However, \nthis is prone to change and the whims of the upper ridge.  \"Cooler\" \ntemperatures over the weekend should negate the need for Heat \nAdvisories after today, but they'll be back in play Monday through \nthe extended.  Rain chances will be minimal, and typical for late \nJuly.",
